-- Quest reward itemization, ruling 21 (docs/plans/quest-reward-itemization/, stage QR1b): Quality 2
-- (Uncommon) rows for item_weapon_dps_curve, so green weapons (and the white quest rewards that become green)
-- can be itemized. Until now the table had Rare (3) and Epic (4) rows only, and ItemBudget.cpp refuses an
-- itemized weapon with no curve row ("no item_weapon_dps_curve entry").
--
-- Derived exactly as 2026_09_05_33.sql derived the Rare/Epic rows (the same script reproduces those rows to
-- within 0.01 DPS for Rare paired and Epic paired): stock weapons from the base dump (entry <= 56806, class 2,
-- Quality 2, delay > 0, dmg_max1 > 0) with a Str/Agi/AttackPower stat column and no Int/Spirit/SpellPower one;
-- per hand category (is_single_slot 1 = Two-Hand/Ranged/Thrown/Relic, 0 = the rest), DPS = avg(dmg_min1,
-- dmg_max1) / (delay / 1000); median per ItemLevel; sample-size-weighted isotonic regression (PAVA); linear
-- interpolation between fitted points, flat past the real range; ilvl 1-300.
-- Paired: 153 weapons, 56 item levels, real range ilvl 11-174.
-- Single slot: 158 weapons, 53 item levels, real range ilvl 10-174.
-- Clamp (mirror of the Epic >= Rare clamp): green never above Rare at the same (ilvl, is_single_slot); it binds
-- at 35 single-slot item levels in 131-170 (TBC range, sparse green data) and nowhere on the paired curve.
--
-- Also bumps item_budget_version 2 -> 3 (operator bookkeeping: item caches may be stale), as
-- 2026_09_05_38.sql did.
--
DELETE FROM `item_weapon_dps_curve` WHERE `quality` = 2;

DELETE FROM `item_budget_version` WHERE `id` = 1;
